PROBLEM DATA
BOOK: Problem data
TITLE: Units
QUESTION: Mesh_units#CB#(m,cm,mm)
VALUE: m
HELP: Choose the units for the mesh dimensions
QUESTION: Results_units#CB#(N-m-kg,N-cm-kg,N-mm-kg,Kp-cm-utm,kN-m-MPa-ton)
VALUE: N-m-kg
HELP: Choose the units for the results to postprocess after calculation
TITLE: Gravity
QUESTION: Gravity_X:
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Choose the direction of the gravity for problems with Specific Weight != 0
QUESTION: Gravity_Y:
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Choose the direction of the gravity for problems with Specific Weight != 0
QUESTION: Gravity_Z:
VALUE: -1.0
HELP: Choose the direction of the gravity for problems with Specific Weight != 0
TITLE: Results
QUESTION: Beam_Res_granularity:
VALUE: 20
HELP: Results graphics for beams will have this number of segments precision.
QUESTION: Shell_Res_axes#CB#(Both,Local_axes,Main_axes)
VALUE: Both
HELP: Results for shells can be given in:\n   Local Axes: the ones defined in the\n     preprocess in the shell condition\n   Main Axes: the main axes calculated for axial\n     strengths and the main axes calculated\n     for momentus
QUESTION: Output_shell_stresses#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: no
HELP: If this option is set, program will output the stresses and Von-Misses stress for the superior and inferior faces of the shell.
QUESTION: Output_beams_maximums#CB#(Automatic,Never,Always)
VALUE: Automatic
HELP: When there are more than one loadcase, it is possible to output a special loadcase containing the maximums for beams. Option 'Automatic', outputs it only if there are steel sections. Option 'Always', output it if there are more than one loadcase.
QUESTION: Shell_Internal_6-noded_elem#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: 3-noded triangle shell elements are calculated internally as 6-noded elements.
QUESTION: Shell_Smooth_Res#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: If Smooth results is set, strengths are smoothed by zones
TITLE: Analysis
QUESTION: Problem_type#CB#(Beams_and_shells,Plane_strain,Plane_stress,Plates)
VALUE: Beams_and_shells
HELP: 'Plane stress' and 'Plates' are particular cases of 'Beams and shells'. Its only advantage is that they are faster. Input data and results are equal than 'Beams and shells'. 'Plane strain' substitutes the stress case for the strain case. In 'Plane strain', the Thickness of the shell is not considered.
QUESTION: Consider_beam_P-Delta#CB#(0,1)
VALUE: 0
HELP: When activated, P-Delta analysis is performed. This analysis considers the second order effects in the beams
QUESTION: Analysis_Type#CB#(Linear_Static,Linear_Dynamic,Non-Linear_Static,Non-Linear_Dynamic)
VALUE: Linear_Static
HELP: Define the type of analysis to perform.Linear_Static
DEPENDENCIES: (Linear_Static,HIDE,DUMMY_atype,Linear_Static)              (Linear_Dynamic,HIDE,DUMMY_atype,Linear_Dynamic)              (Non-Linear_Static,HIDE,DUMMY_atype,Non-Linear_Static)              (Non-Linear_Dynamic,HIDE,DUMMY_atype,Non-Linear-Dynamic)
QUESTION: DUMMY_atype
VALUE: Linear_Static
TKWIDGET: ProblemDataWidget::Analysis_windows
STATE: HIDDEN
QUESTION: Activate_Load_Cases#CB#(none,independent,combined)
VALUE: none
STATE: HIDDEN
QUESTION: Combined_load_cases:(name,isstrength,loads)
VALUE: #N# 3 Combined_1 1 allone
STATE: HIDDEN
BOOK: Linear_Dynamic
TITLE: General
QUESTION: Dynamic_Analysis_Type#CB#(Modal_Analysis,Direct_Integration,Spectrum_Analysis)
VALUE: Modal_Analysis
HELP: Choose the type of Dynamic Analysis that Ram-Series will perform
DEPENDENCIES: (Direct_Integration,HIDE,Number_of_Modes,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Damping_Type,Rayleigh_Damping,                 RESTORE,Matrix_storage,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Gamma,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Beta,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,DeltaT,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Number_of_steps,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Spectrum_Analysis_type,#CURRENT#,                 TITLESTATE,Seismic_data,hidden,                 TITLESTATE,U.D._spectrum,hidden,                 RESTORE,Initial_Conditions:,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE, __DUMMY2_, direct)             (Modal_Analysis,RESTORE,Number_of_Modes,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Gamma,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Beta,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Matrix_storage,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Damping_Type,->Damping_Type,                 RESTORE,DeltaT,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Number_of_steps,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Spectrum_Analysis_type,#CURRENT#,                 TITLESTATE,Seismic_data,hidden,                 TITLESTATE,U.D._spectrum,hidden,                 RESTORE,Initial_Conditions:,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE, __DUMMY2__, modal)             (Spectrum_Analysis,RESTORE,Number_of_Modes,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Gamma,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Beta,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Matrix_storage,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Damping_Type,Modal_Damping,                 HIDE,DeltaT,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Number_of_steps,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Spectrum_Analysis_type,->Spectrum_Analysis_type,                 HIDE,Initial_Conditions:,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE, __DUMMY2__, spectrum)
QUESTION: Number_of_Modes
VALUE: 1
HELP: Choose the number of modes to consider in the Modal Analysis
QUESTION: DeltaT
VALUE: 0.01
HELP: Time increment for the dynamic analysis
QUESTION: Number_of_steps
VALUE: 10
HELP: Number of steps of the dynamic analysis.\nTotal physical time will be Number_of_Steps X Delta_T.
QUESTION: Gamma
VALUE: 0.5
HELP: Parameter for the direct integration
QUESTION: Beta
VALUE: 0.25
HELP: Parameter for the direct integration
QUESTION: Matrix_storage#CB#(Lumped,Consistent)
VALUE: Lumped
DEPENDENCIES: (Lumped,SET,Alpha_K,0.0)             (Consistent,RESTORE,Damping_Type,#CURRENT#)
HELP: Choose the type of storage for the Mass and Damping Matrix. If Lumped Matrix storage is choose, the  part of the Damping Matrix related with the stiffness matrix is neglected  (Alpha_K=0).
QUESTION: Damping_Type#CB#(Modal_Damping,Rayleigh_Damping)
VALUE: Modal_Damping
HELP: Choose the type of damping used in the analysis. There are two types avaible: Modal damping and Rayleigh damping
DEPENDENCIES: (Modal_Damping,RESTORE,Damping_ratio,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Alpha_M,#CURRENT#,                 HIDE,Alpha_K,#CURRENT#)             (Rayleigh_Damping,HIDE,Damping_ratio,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Alpha_M,#CURRENT#,                 RESTORE,Alpha_K,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Damping_ratio
VALUE: 0.05
HELP: Express the damping as a ratio of the critical damping ratio
QUESTION: Alpha_M
VALUE: 0.1
HELP: Coefficient of the Mass Matrix in the Rayleigh Damping
QUESTION: Alpha_K
VALUE: 0.1
HELP: Coefficient of the Stiffness Matrix in the Rayleigh Damping
QUESTION: Spectrum_Analysis_type#CB#(Seismic_codes,User_defined_spectrum)
VALUE: Seismic_codes
HELP: Choose the type of Spectrum Analysis used in the analysis. There are two types avaible: Seismic codes and User define spectrum.
DEPENDENCIES: (Seismic_codes,TITLESTATE,Seismic_data,normal,                 TITLESTATE,U.D._spectrum,hidden)             (User_defined_spectrum,TITLESTATE,Seismic_data,hidden,                 TITLESTATE,U.D._spectrum,normal)
QUESTION: Initial_Conditions:#CB#(None,Comb._Load_1,User_Defined)
VALUE: None
HELP: None: No assign any intial conditions \nComb._Load_1: Assign like initial conditions an static combinated load case \nUser_Defined: Assign initial conditions defined by the user
QUESTION: __DUMMY2__
VALUE: direct
STATE: HIDDEN
DEPENDENCIES: (direct, -)(modal,                  TITLESTATE,Seismic_data,hidden,                 TITLESTATE,U.D._spectrum,hidden)
TITLE: Seismic_data
QUESTION: Code_type#CB#(NCSE-94_Spain_Code,Other)
VALUE: NCSE-94_Spain_Code
HELP: Indicate de the seismic code used.
QUESTION: Design_Seismic_Acceleration
VALUE: 5.0
HELP: Indicate de the design seismic acceleration proposed in the code
QUESTION: Seismic_direction_nx
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the seismic in the x global direction
QUESTION: Seismic_direction_ny
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the seismic in the y global direction
QUESTION: Seismic_direction_nz
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the seismic in the z global direction
QUESTION: Soil_coefficient
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Soil coefficient defined in the code
QUESTION: Contribution_coefficient
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Contribution coefficient defined in the code
QUESTION: Ductility
VALUE: 2.0
HELP: Structure ductility defined in the code
TITLE: U.D._spectrum
QUESTION: Spectrum_Table:(T[seg],Sa[m/seg2])
VALUE: #N# 2 0.0 0.0
QUESTION: Spectrum_direction_nx
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the spectrum in the x global direction
QUESTION: Spectrum_direction_ny
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the spectrum in the y global direction
QUESTION: Spectrum_direction_nz
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Indicate the component of the spectrum in the z global direction
BOOK: Non-Linear_Static
TITLE: General
QUESTION: Delta_Fac
VALUE: 6.0
HELP: Is the initial value of the incremetal load factor or displacement factor. If the arc-lenght method is to be adopted       and the "desired lenght",Delta_Ld, for the first increment is input as zero, then Delta_P is       automatically converted to a "length".
QUESTION: Num_inc
VALUE: 10
HELP: Is the desired number of increment.
QUESTION: Automatic_inc#CB#(Yes,No)
VALUE: Yes
HELP: If this parameter is set to "Yes", automatic increment sizes are computed.       Such automatic increments increments must be used with the arc-length method. \n       If is set to "No", equal increments of magnitude Delta_P are adopted.
DEPENDENCIES: (No,TITLESTATE,Automatic_inc,hidden)             (Yes,TITLESTATE,Automatic_inc,normal)
QUESTION: Control#CB#(Load_Control,Disp._Control,Arc-lenght_Control)
VALUE: Load_Control
HELP: Define the type of control for the non linear analysis.
DEPENDENCIES: (Arc-lenght_Control,TITLESTATE,Arc-Length,normal)             (Load_Control,TITLESTATE,Arc-Length,hidden)             (Disp._Control,TITLESTATE,Arc-Length,hidden)
QUESTION: Conv._tolerance
VALUE: 0.001
HELP: Convergence tolerance factor.
QUESTION: Iteration_type#CB#(Full_N-R,Modified_N-R)
VALUE: Full_N-R
HELP: Indicate if the full or modified Newton Raphson method is choseen.
QUESTION: Max_iter
VALUE: 10
HELP: Define the maximun number of iterations
QUESTION: Line-Search#CB#(Yes,No)
VALUE: No
HELP: Define if line search method are required
DEPENDENCIES: (No,TITLESTATE,Line-Search,hidden)             (Yes,TITLESTATE,Line-Search,normal)
QUESTION: Auto-ARC-switch#CB#(Yes,No)
VALUE: No
HELP: Automatic switch to the arc-length method.
DEPENDENCIES: (No,TITLESTATE,Auto-ARC-switch,hidden)             (Yes,TITLESTATE,Auto-ARC-switch,normal)
TITLE: Line-Search
QUESTION: LS-loops
VALUE: 10
HELP: Define the maximun number of Line-Search loops.
QUESTION: LS-toler
VALUE: 0.8
HELP: Tolerance on ratio.
QUESTION: LS-min
VALUE: 0.1
HELP: Define the minim step-length of Line-Search.
QUESTION: LS-max
VALUE: 1.5
HELP: Define the maxim step-length of Line-Search.
QUESTION: Amp-max
VALUE: 1.5
HELP: Define the maxim amplitude of any step.
TITLE: Automatic_inc
QUESTION: Num_Iter_d
VALUE: 3
HELP: Number of iteration desired.
QUESTION: DeltaP_max
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Maxim load increment.
QUESTION: DeltaP_min
VALUE: 1.0
HELP: Minim load increment.
TITLE: Auto-ARC-switch
QUESTION: C_Stif
VALUE: 0.3
HELP: The desired current stiffness parameter for swithching.
TITLE: Arc-Length
QUESTION: DeltaL_d
VALUE: 0.05
HELP: Desired lenght increment.
QUESTION: DeltaL_max
VALUE: 0.05
HELP: Maxim lenght increment.
QUESTION: DeltaL_min
VALUE: 0.05
HELP: Minim lenght increment.
BOOK: Non-Linear-Dynamic
TITLE: General
QUESTION: Integration_method#CB#(Implicit,Explicit)
VALUE: Implicit
HELP: Algorithm of temporal integration
DEPENDENCIES: (Implicit,TITLESTATE,Integration_Data,normal,                       TITLESTATE,Non-Linear,normal,                       HIDE,Delta_T,#CURRENT#,		       HIDE,Number-of-steps,#CURRENT#,                       RESTORE,DeltaT_variation,#CURRENT#)	     (Explicit,TITLESTATE,Integration_Data,hidden,                       TITLESTATE,Non-Linear,hidden,                       RESTORE,Matrix-storage,Lumped,                       RESTORE,Delta_T,#CURRENT#,		       RESTORE,Number-of-steps,#CURRENT#,                       HIDE,DeltaT_variation,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: T_0
VALUE: 0.0
HELP: Initial time for the dynamic analysis.
QUESTION: Delta_T
VALUE: 0.01
HELP: Time increment for the dynamic analysis
QUESTION: Number-of-steps
VALUE: 10
HELP: Number of steps of the dynamic analysis.\nTotal physical time will be Number_of_Steps X Delta_T.
QUESTION: DeltaT_variation:(Amount_of_steps,DeltaT)
VALUE: #N# 2 10   0.01
HELP: Time increment variation for certain number of step.
QUESTION: Matrix-storage#CB#(Lumped,Consistent)
VALUE: Lumped
HELP: Choose the type of storage for the Mass and Damping Matrix.
QUESTION: Initial_Conditions#CB#(None,Comb._Load_1,User_Defined)
VALUE: None
HELP: None: No assign any intial conditions \nComb._Load_1: Assign like initial conditions an the static linear elastic state in Combinated Load Case\nUser_Defined: Assign initial conditions defined by the user
DEPENDENCIES: (None,HIDE,Comb._Load_1_data,#CURRENT#)			  (Comb._Load_1,RESTORE,Comb._Load_1_data,#CURRENT#)			  (User_Defined,HIDE,Comb._Load_1_data,#CURRENT#)
QUESTION: Comb._Load_1_data#CB#(Only_disp,Disp_and_load)
VALUE: Disp_and_load
HELP: This question indicate wich data are pass like initial condition in the Non linear dynamic analysis
TITLE: Integration_Data
QUESTION: Gamma:
VALUE: 0.5
HELP: Parameter for the direct integration
QUESTION: Beta:
VALUE: 0.25
HELP: Parameter for the direct integration
TITLE: Damping
QUESTION: Alpha_M:
VALUE: 0.1
QUESTION: Alpha_K:
VALUE: 0.1
HELP: Coefficient of the Mass Matrix in the Rayleigh Damping
TITLE: Non-Linear
QUESTION: Conv._tolerance
VALUE: 0.001
HELP: Convergence tolerance factor.
QUESTION: Iteration-type#CB#(Full_N-R,Modif_1_N-R,Modif_2_N-R,Initial_N-R)
VALUE: Full_N-R
HELP: Indicate if the full,modified o intial Newton Raphson method is choseen.
QUESTION: Max-iter
VALUE: 10
HELP: Define the maximun number of iterations
BOOK: Advanced
TITLE: Solver
QUESTION: Solver_type#CB#(Automatic,SkyLine,Sparse)
VALUE: Automatic
DEPENDENCIES: (Sparse,RESTORE,Solver_tolerance,#CURRENT#,                  RESTORE,Solver_tolerance_minimum,#CURRENT#,                  RESTORE,Solver_max_iterations,#CURRENT#)
DEPENDENCIES: (#DEFAULT#,HIDE,Solver_tolerance,#CURRENT#,                  HIDE,Solver_tolerance_minimum,#CURRENT#,                  HIDE,Solver_max_iterations,#CURRENT#)
HELP: Permmits to choose the solver to be used:\nAtomatic: Runs a direct solver for small problems and an iterative for big ones.\nSkyLine: Direct solver. It has no convergence problems but needs more RAM memory.\nSparse: Iterative solver. they take much less memory but may not converge. User can choose desired parameters.
QUESTION: Solver_tolerance
VALUE: 1.0e-5
HELP: Tolerance accepted to finish iterations
QUESTION: Solver_tolerance_minimum
VALUE: 1.0e-1
HELP: If solver arrives to Max iterations, then this tolerance is used to accept or not the result.
QUESTION: Solver_max_iterations
VALUE: 20000
HELP: Maximum number of iterations permmited to the solver.
TITLE: Eigen_Solver
QUESTION: Eigensolver_max_iterations
VALUE: 16
HELP: Maximum number of iterations permmited to the eigensolver.
TITLE: Dynamic_Output
QUESTION: Write_Displacements#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: Indicate if Displacements are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Write_Velocities#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: no
HELP: Indicate if Velocities are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Write_Accelerations#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: no
HELP: Indicate if Accelerations are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Write_Strengths#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: Indicate if Strengths are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Write_Reactions#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: Indicate if Reactions are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Write_ElemDamage#CB#(yes,no)
VALUE: yes
HELP: Indicate if the elemental damage are required in the postprocess
QUESTION: Output_Step
VALUE: 1
HELP: Each Output_Step time steps the results will be written.
BOOK: Integration sections
QUESTION: Shell_integration_sections:(Name,x1,y1,z1,x2,y2,z2)
VALUE: #N# 1 -
STATE: HIDDEN
HELP: Permmits to define a section over one shell part. Results will be integrated on the section and output to the details file
TKWIDGET: shell_sections::ComunicateWithGiD
END PROBLEM DATA
